      },
      "description": [
        {
          "text": "This family of proteins includes enzymes with sugar-1-kinase activity, specifically recognizing D-glucuronic acid and ATP as substrates. Members of this family are involved in the biosynthesis of UDP-glucuronic acid (UDP-GlcA), which is a precursor for nucleotide sugars required in the assembly of cell-wall polymers. Additionally, these proteins may participate in the recycling of glucuronic acid through a salvage pathway.",
